{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/connect.cljc | sed -n '1,430p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.connect\n     2\t  \"The client side of the DaoStream Yin REPL, over the request-and-response\n     3\t   service of docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md section 5.\n     4\t\n     5\t   One connection is one explicit value.  `open` canonicalizes the URL to the\n     6\t   request-target form `dao.stream.ws.md` defines, dials one WebSocket\n     7\t   channel through `dao.stream.ws-project`, and attaches two\n     8\t   `dao.stream.remote` reflections over it -- one of `\\\"yin.repl/requests\\\"`\n     9\t   (this end writes), one of `\\\"yin.repl/answers\\\"` (this end reads) -- both\n    10\t   sharing the one link the dial establishes.  `attach!` over\n    11\t   `dao.stream.remote` answers ok at once: that is the contract's deferred\n    12\t   remote confirmation, not a promise that the server has resolved anything,\n    13\t   so a connection is reported `:established` immediately rather than\n    14\t   waiting on an asynchronous transport event.\n    15\t\n    16\t   The dial is reusable across reconnects: `close!` closes the underlying\n    17\t   channel handle, and reattaching redials the same `attach!` and repeats\n    18\t   both reflection attaches, then `rpc/rebind`s the retained RPC client onto\n    19\t   the fresh pair -- which keeps its response cursor and its outstanding\n    20\t   bookkeeping, exactly as before.  Terminal status\n    21\t   (`:detached`/`:ended`/`:not-found`/`:transport-error`) is observed from\n    22\t   the RPC client's own `:terminal`, translated by `dao.stream.rpc`'s\n    23\t   reflection-read translation; `observe-terminal` turns that into the one\n    24\t   connection notice each terminal reason publishes exactly once.\"\n    25\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    26\t            [dao.data :as data]\n    27\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    28\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    29\t            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n    30\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n    31\t            [dao.stream.ws-project :as ws-project]\n    32\t            [yin.repl.host.common :as host-common]))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t;; =============================================================================\n    36\t;; Composition constants\n    37\t;; =============================================================================\n    38\t\n    39\t(def traffic-capacity\n    40\t  \"Declared capacity of the boundary's one traffic medium, in elements.  It is\n    41\t   reused across reconnects because a client boundary has at most one active\n    42\t   attachment at a time.\"\n    43\t  8192)\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(def traffic-admission\n    47\t  {:retention :evict-oldest\n    48\t   :capacity traffic-capacity\n    49\t   :value-domain :portable-values})\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(def url-prefix \"daostream:\")\n    53\t(def ws-scheme \"ws://\")\n    54\t(def secure-scheme \"wss://\")\n    55\t(def default-port 8080)\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(def repl-path\n    59\t  \"The path an empty URL path means for this REPL (D3).  An explicit `/`\n    60\t   remains `/`; only an absent path becomes the served REPL stream.\"\n    61\t  \"/repl\")\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(def service-identity\n    65\t  \"The logical identity of the WebSocket channel a REPL endpoint serves.  A\n    66\t   descriptor names a served stream, so a client that only typed a URL still\n    67\t   needs one; a stable service name keeps `attach!` honest across endpoint\n    68\t   restarts.\"\n    69\t  \"yin.repl/repl\")\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t(def requests-identity\n    73\t  \"The mirror table identity the server enters with surface #{:writer}: a\n    74\t   client's reflection of it writes eval requests.\"\n    75\t  \"yin.repl/requests\")\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(def answers-identity\n    79\t  \"The mirror table identity the server enters with surface #{:reader}: a\n    80\t   client's reflection of it reads answers.\"\n    81\t  \"yin.repl/answers\")\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t(def ^:private diagnostic-bounds\n    85\t  \"Bound on operator-facing diagnostic text built from unbounded internal\n    86\t   state (raw connect URLs).\"\n    87\t  {:depth 3 :items 8 :chars 200})\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(def outcome-key :yin.repl.connect/outcome)\n    91\t(def connection-key :yin.repl.connect/connection)\n    92\t(def client-key :yin.repl.connect/client)\n    93\t(def descriptor-key :yin.repl.connect/descriptor)\n    94\t(def message-key :yin.repl.connect/message)\n    95\t(def event-key :yin.repl.connect/event)\n    96\t(def text-key :yin.repl.connect/text)\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t;; =============================================================================\n   100\t;; Canonical request-target paths\n   101\t;; =============================================================================\n   102\t\n   103\t(def ^:private ascii-printable\n   104\t  \" !\\\"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[\\\\]^_`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz{|}~\")\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t(def ^:private unreserved\n   108\t  (set (map str (seq \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789-._~\"))))\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\t(def ^:private hex-values\n   112\t  (merge (zipmap (map str (seq \"0123456789\")) (range 10))\n   113\t         (zipmap (map str (seq \"abcdef\")) (range 10 16))\n   114\t         (zipmap (map str (seq \"ABCDEF\")) (range 10 16))))\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(def ^:private digits (set (map str (seq \"0123456789\"))))\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(defn- at\n   121\t  \"One character of `s` as a one-character string, so nothing here depends on a\n   122\t   host's character representation.\"\n   123\t  [s i]\n   124\t  (subs s i (inc i)))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn- octet->char\n   128\t  [code]\n   129\t  (when (and (<= 32 code) (<= code 126))\n   130\t    (subs ascii-printable (- code 32) (- code 31))))\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\t(defn- percent-canonical\n   134\t  \"Decode percent-encoded unreserved octets and upper-case every remaining\n   135\t   percent hex pair.  An encoded slash is not unreserved, so it stays encoded.\"\n   136\t  [s]\n   137\t  (let [n (count s)]\n   138\t    (loop [i 0\n   139\t           out []]\n   140\t      (if (>= i n)\n   141\t        (str/join out)\n   142\t        (let [c (at s i)\n   143\t              hi (when (< (+ i 2) n) (get hex-values (at s (+ i 1))))\n   144\t              lo (when (< (+ i 2) n) (get hex-values (at s (+ i 2))))]\n   145\t          (if (and (= \"%\" c) hi lo)\n   146\t            (let [decoded (octet->char (+ (* 16 hi) lo))]\n   147\t              (if (contains? unreserved decoded)\n   148\t                (recur (+ i 3) (conj out decoded))\n   149\t                (recur (+ i 3) (conj out (str \"%\" (str/upper-case (subs s (inc i) (+ i 3))))))))\n   150\t            (recur (inc i) (conj out c))))))))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn- drop-last-segment\n   154\t  [out]\n   155\t  (if-let [i (str/last-index-of out \"/\")]\n   156\t    (subs out 0 i)\n   157\t    \"\"))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t(defn- next-segment-end\n   161\t  [s]\n   162\t  (or (str/index-of s \"/\" 1) (count s)))\n   163\t\n   164\t\n   165\t(defn- remove-dot-segments\n   166\t  \"RFC 3986's remove_dot_segments, so repeated slashes and a trailing slash stay\n   167\t   significant while `.` and `..` do not reach the exact served-path lookup.\"\n   168\t  [path]\n   169\t  (loop [in path\n   170\t         out \"\"]\n   171\t    (cond\n   172\t      (= \"\" in) out\n   173\t      (str/starts-with? in \"../\") (recur (subs in 3) out)\n   174\t      (str/starts-with? in \"./\") (recur (subs in 2) out)\n   175\t      (str/starts-with? in \"/./\") (recur (str \"/\" (subs in 3)) out)\n   176\t      (= \"/.\" in) (recur \"/\" out)\n   177\t      (str/starts-with? in \"/../\") (recur (str \"/\" (subs in 4)) (drop-last-segment out))\n   178\t      (= \"/..\" in) (recur \"/\" (drop-last-segment out))\n   179\t      (= \".\" in) (recur \"\" out)\n   180\t      (= \"..\" in) (recur \"\" out)\n   181\t      :else (let [end (next-segment-end in)]\n   182\t              (recur (subs in end) (str out (subs in 0 end)))))))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn- path-component\n   186\t  \"The URI path component of `raw`: everything before the first query or\n   187\t   fragment delimiter.\"\n   188\t  [raw]\n   189\t  (let [raw (str raw)\n   190\t        cut (->> [(str/index-of raw \"?\") (str/index-of raw \"#\")]\n   191\t                 (filter some?)\n   192\t                 (reduce min (count raw)))]\n   193\t    (subs raw 0 cut)))\n   194\t\n   195\t\n   196\t(defn canonical-path\n   197\t  \"The canonical, non-empty absolute request-target path of `raw`.\n   198\t\n   199\t   Query and fragment are ignored for lookup and absent from the descriptor,\n   200\t   dot segments are removed, percent-encoded unreserved octets are decoded, and\n   201\t   remaining percent hex digits are upper-case.  An empty URI path becomes `/`;\n   202\t   substituting the REPL's own default for an absent path is `repl-target`'s\n   203\t   job, and happens before this generic canonicalizer runs.\"\n   204\t  [raw]\n   205\t  (let [path (path-component raw)\n   206\t        path (if (str/starts-with? path \"/\") path (str \"/\" path))\n   207\t        path (percent-canonical (remove-dot-segments path))]\n   208\t    (if (= \"\" path) \"/\" path)))\n   209\t\n   210\t\n   211\t(defn repl-target\n   212\t  \"The REPL wrapper's rule: an empty raw URL path names `/repl`, and an explicit\n   213\t   `/` remains `/`.  Emptiness is a fact about the URI path component, so\n   214\t   `ws://host:port?x=1` carries no path and names `/repl` too.\"\n   215\t  [raw]\n   216\t  (if (= \"\" (path-component raw))\n   217\t    repl-path\n   218\t    (canonical-path raw)))\n   219\t\n   220\t\n   221\t;; =============================================================================\n   222\t;; URL to descriptor\n   223\t;; =============================================================================\n   224\t\n   225\t(defn- failure\n   226\t  [outcome message]\n   227\t  {outcome-key outcome message-key message})\n   228\t\n   229\t\n   230\t(defn- parse-port\n   231\t  [text]\n   232\t  (when (and (seq text) (every? #(contains? digits %) (map str (seq text))))\n   233\t    (loop [i 0 acc 0]\n   234\t      (if (>= i (count text))\n   235\t        (when (pos? acc) acc)\n   236\t        (recur (inc i) (+ (* 10 acc) (get hex-values (at text i))))))))\n   237\t\n   238\t\n   239\t(defn- authority-end\n   240\t  [s]\n   241\t  (->> [(str/index-of s \"/\") (str/index-of s \"?\") (str/index-of s \"#\")]\n   242\t       (filter some?)\n   243\t       (reduce min (count s))))\n   244\t\n   245\t\n   246\t(defn parse-url\n   247\t  \"Parse one REPL connect URL into a WebSocket descriptor.\n   248\t\n   249\t   Accepted forms are `daostream:ws://host[:port][/path]` and the same URL\n   250\t   without the `daostream:` prefix.  Bracketed IPv6 literals are out of this\n   251\t   slice and are reported rather than silently mis-parsed.\"\n   252\t  ([url] (parse-url url {}))\n   253\t  ([url {:keys [identity]}]\n   254\t   (let [url (str/trim (str url))\n   255\t         body (if (str/starts-with? url url-prefix) (subs url (count url-prefix)) url)]\n   256\t     (cond\n   257\t       (str/starts-with? body secure-scheme)\n   258\t       (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   259\t                \"wss:// has no settled descriptor form in this slice; use ws://\")\n   260\t\n   261\t       (not (str/starts-with? body ws-scheme))\n   262\t       (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   263\t                (str \"connect needs a daostream:ws:// URL; got \"\n   264\t                     (pr-str (data/summarize url diagnostic-bounds))))\n   265\t\n   266\t       :else\n   267\t       (let [rest-url (subs body (count ws-scheme))\n   268\t             end (authority-end rest-url)\n   269\t             authority (subs rest-url 0 end)\n   270\t             raw-path (subs rest-url end)\n   271\t             colon (str/last-index-of authority \":\")\n   272\t             host (if colon (subs authority 0 colon) authority)\n   273\t             port (if colon (parse-port (subs authority (inc colon))) default-port)]\n   274\t         (cond\n   275\t           (str/starts-with? authority \"[\")\n   276\t           (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   277\t                    \"bracketed IPv6 authorities are not part of this slice\")\n   278\t\n   279\t           (str/blank? host)\n   280\t           (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   281\t                    (str \"connect URL has no host: \"\n   282\t                         (pr-str (data/summarize url diagnostic-bounds))))\n   283\t\n   284\t           (nil? port)\n   285\t           (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   286\t                    (str \"connect URL port must be a positive integer: \"\n   287\t                         (pr-str (data/summarize url diagnostic-bounds))))\n   288\t\n   289\t           :else\n   290\t           (let [descriptor {:dao.stream/type ws/transport-type\n   291\t                             :dao.stream/identity (or identity service-identity)\n   292\t                             :ws/host host\n   293\t                             :ws/port port\n   294\t                             :ws/path (repl-target raw-path)}]\n   295\t             (if (ws/descriptor? descriptor)\n   296\t               {outcome-key :yin.repl.connect/parsed descriptor-key descriptor}\n   297\t               (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   298\t                        (str \"connect URL does not name a servable stream: \"\n   299\t                             (pr-str (data/summarize url diagnostic-bounds))))))))))))\n   300\t\n   301\t\n   302\t;; =============================================================================\n   303\t;; The two-reflection boundary\n   304\t;; =============================================================================\n   305\t\n   306\t(defn- mint\n   307\t  [handle anchor]\n   308\t  (let [result (stream/cursor handle anchor)]\n   309\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n   310\t      (:dao.stream/cursor result))))\n   311\t\n   312\t\n   313\t(defn- remote-descriptor\n   314\t  [channel identity]\n   315\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n   316\t   :dao.stream/identity identity\n   317\t   :dao.stream/channel channel})\n   318\t\n   319\t\n   320\t(defn- attacher\n   321\t  [traffic connect!]\n   322\t  (ws/make-attacher {:traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic\n   323\t                               :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   324\t                     :admission traffic-admission\n   325\t                     :connect! connect!}))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn- attach-outcome-message\n   329\t  [url result]\n   330\t  (case (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   331\t    :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor\n   332\t    (str \"The boundary refused the descriptor for \" url)\n   333\t\n   334\t    :dao.stream/transport-error\n   335\t    (str \"Could not start connecting to \" url\n   336\t         \"; this is a local reachability failure and may succeed on retry\")\n   337\t\n   338\t    (str \"Attaching to \" url \" answered \" (pr-str (:dao.stream/outcome result)))))\n   339\t\n   340\t\n   341\t(defn- fresh-dial\n   342\t  \"Compose one dial over a fresh traffic medium, its own fresh `attach!`\n   343\t   bound to that medium, and a fresh channel ring, before any attach.  A\n   344\t   reattachment composes a fresh dial with a fresh cursor, per\n   345\t   `dao.stream.ws-project/dial`'s own contract, and `attach!` is scoped to\n   346\t   the traffic medium it deposits into, so it must be rebuilt alongside\n   347\t   it -- reusing an old `attach!` over a new traffic medium would deposit\n   348\t   into the wrong buffer.\"\n   349\t  [host]\n   350\t  (let [traffic (:dao.stream/handle\n   351\t                  (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n   352\t                                 ring/capacity-key traffic-capacity}))\n   353\t        attach! (try (attacher traffic (:connect! host))\n   354\t                     (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))\n   355\t        cursor (mint traffic stream/anchor-newest)\n   356\t        ring (:dao.stream/handle\n   357\t               (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n   358\t                              ring/capacity-key traffic-capacity}))]\n   359\t    (when (and (some? attach!) (some? cursor))\n   360\t      (ws-project/dial {:attach! attach!\n   361\t                        :traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic}\n   362\t                        :cursor cursor\n   363\t                        :ring ring\n   364\t                        :table {}}))))\n   365\t\n   366\t\n   367\t(defn- attach-pair\n   368\t  \"Attach both `requests`/`answers` reflections through `dial`'s one link,\n   369\t   sharing it exactly as `dao.stream.remote.cljc`'s attacher requires.\n   370\t   Returns `[requests-result answers-result]`, the second nil once the\n   371\t   first fails.\"\n   372\t  [dial channel]\n   373\t  (let [requests-result\n   374\t        (ws-project/dial-attach! dial (remote-descriptor channel\n   375\t                                                          requests-identity))]\n   376\t    (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome requests-result))\n   377\t      [requests-result nil]\n   378\t      [requests-result\n   379\t       (ws-project/dial-reflect! dial (remote-descriptor channel\n   380\t                                                          answers-identity))])))\n   381\t\n   382\t\n   383\t(defn open\n   384\t  \"Dial one WebSocket channel and attach both reflections, returning\n   385\t   immediately.  `attach!` over `dao.stream.remote` answers ok at once --\n   386\t   the contract's deferred remote confirmation -- so a successful result\n   387\t   is reported `:established` without waiting on any further transport\n   388\t   event.  The RPC client's response cursor is the `:dao.stream/newest`\n   389\t   anchor; `rpc/poll!` resolves it, retrying while the answers reflection\n   390\t   answers a retryable mint.\"\n   391\t  [{:keys [url identity host]}]\n   392\t  (let [parsed (parse-url url {:identity identity})]\n   393\t    (if-not (= :yin.repl.connect/parsed (get parsed outcome-key))\n   394\t      parsed\n   395\t      (let [channel (get parsed descriptor-key)]\n   396\t        (if-not (host-common/adapter? host)\n   397\t          (failure :yin.repl.connect/no-host-adapter\n   398\t                   (host-common/missing-message \"(connect …) is not wired\"))\n   399\t          (let [dial (fresh-dial host)]\n   400\t            (if-not dial\n   401\t              (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-composition\n   402\t                       \"The client boundary composition was refused\")\n   403\t              (let [[requests-result answers-result]\n   404\t                    (attach-pair dial channel)]\n   405\t                (cond\n   406\t                  (not= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome requests-result))\n   407\t                  (failure :yin.repl.connect/attach-failed\n   408\t                           (attach-outcome-message url requests-result))\n   409\t\n   410\t                  (not= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answers-result))\n   411\t                  (failure :yin.repl.connect/attach-failed\n   412\t                           (attach-outcome-message url answers-result))\n   413\t\n   414\t                  :else\n   415\t                  {outcome-key :yin.repl.connect/attached\n   416\t                   connection-key {:url url\n   417\t                                   :channel channel\n   418\t                                   :host host\n   419\t                                   :dial dial\n   420\t                                   :status :established\n   421\t                                   :detached-by nil}\n   422\t                   client-key (rpc/client-state\n   423\t                                (:dao.stream/handle requests-result)\n   424\t                                (:dao.stream/handle answers-result)\n   425\t                                stream/anchor-newest)})))))))))\n   426\t\n   427\t\n   428\t(defn step!\n   429\t  \"Drive this connection's dial one tick: its projection, so wire bytes the\n   430\t   host deposited onto the traffic medium reach the reflections' local\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc.cljc | sed -n '365,650p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/serve.cljc | sed -n '380,750p'\"","aggregated_output":"   365\t(defn handle-event\n   366\t  \"Apply one decoded RPC event to explicit client state.\n   367\t\n   368\t   `response-event`, `diagnostic-event`, and `ignore-event` are the events a\n   369\t   composition constructs; a bare answer value is also accepted.  This\n   370\t   function has no cursor operation and is useful for testing adapters\n   371\t   independently from a response medium.\"\n   372\t  [state event]\n   373\t  (let [event (normalize-event event)\n   374\t        kind (get event event-key)]\n   375\t    (cond\n   376\t      ;; A terminal binding cannot complete an old request later.  Keep the\n   377\t      ;; event as diagnostic data rather than silently treating it as a reply.\n   378\t      (:terminal state)\n   379\t      (let [state (append-diagnostic state :dao.stream.rpc/event-after-terminal event)]\n   380\t        (rpc-result :dao.stream.rpc/diagnostic state\n   381\t                    :dao.stream.rpc/diagnostic (last (:diagnostics state))))\n   382\t\n   383\t      (= kind :dao.stream.rpc/ignore)\n   384\t      (rpc-result :dao.stream.rpc/ignored state)\n   385\t\n   386\t      (= kind :dao.stream.rpc/diagnostic)\n   387\t      (let [diagnostic (get event diagnostic-key)\n   388\t            state (append-diagnostic state (get diagnostic code-key) diagnostic)]\n   389\t        (rpc-result :dao.stream.rpc/diagnostic state\n   390\t                    :dao.stream.rpc/diagnostic (last (:diagnostics state))))\n   391\t\n   392\t      (= kind :dao.stream.rpc/response)\n   393\t      (let [response (get event response-key)]\n   394\t        (if-not (answer? response)\n   395\t          (handle-event state (diagnostic-event :dao.stream.rpc/malformed-response response))\n   396\t          (let [id (answer-id response)]\n   397\t            (if-let [request (get (:outstanding state) id)]\n   398\t              (let [state (-> state\n   399\t                              (update :outstanding dissoc id)\n   400\t                              (append-completion (assoc request :id id)\n   401\t                                                 :response response))]\n   402\t                (rpc-result :dao.stream.rpc/responded state\n   403\t                            :dao.stream.rpc/id id\n   404\t                            :dao.stream.rpc/response response))\n   405\t              (handle-event state\n   406\t                            (diagnostic-event :dao.stream.rpc/unsolicited-response response))))))\n   407\t\n   408\t      :else\n   409\t      (handle-event state (diagnostic-event :dao.stream.rpc/unhandled-event event)))))\n   410\t\n   411\t\n   412\t(defn- transport-error-reason\n   413\t  \"Translate a reflection's `:dao.stream/transport-error` into the client\n   414\t   terminal vocabulary, inspecting `:dao.stream.remote/reason` when the\n   415\t   reflection supplied one (dao.stream.remote.cljc reasons a reflection's\n   416\t   read failure this way).  A reason this translation does not recognize\n   417\t   still becomes the generic transport-error terminal, never left raw.\"\n   418\t  [read-result]\n   419\t  (case (:dao.stream.remote/reason read-result)\n   420\t    :dao.stream.remote/not-found :dao.stream.apply/not-found\n   421\t    :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone :dao.stream.apply/detached\n   422\t    :dao.stream.apply/transport-error))\n   423\t\n   424\t\n   425\t(defn- terminal-lost\n   426\t  \"Translate a non-ok, non-blocked, non-gap read or mint result into the\n   427\t   client's terminal vocabulary and complete every outstanding request\n   428\t   with it.  Shared by `poll-read`'s `next` failures and `mint-cursor`'s\n   429\t   terminal mint failures, so a reasoned not-found or channel-gone\n   430\t   reaches the terminal the same way regardless of which operation\n   431\t   the reflection answered it to.\"\n   432\t  [state result]\n   433\t  (let [reason (case (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   434\t                 :dao.stream/end :dao.stream.apply/ended\n   435\t                 :dao.stream/transport-error (transport-error-reason result)\n   436\t                 :dao.stream.apply/transport-error)\n   437\t        state (lose-outstanding state reason true)]\n   438\t    (rpc-result :dao.stream.rpc/lost state\n   439\t                :dao.stream.rpc/reason reason\n   440\t                :dao.stream.rpc/read result)))\n   441\t\n   442\t\n   443\t(defn- mint-cursor\n   444\t  \"Resolve an anchor-keyword cursor through the reader.  A retryable\n   445\t   answer -- `:dao.stream/transport-error` carrying `:dao.stream/retry?\n   446\t   true` -- leaves the anchor in place for a later poll (dao.jing.content.\n   447\t   step/mint-cursor is the precedent this mirrors).  Any other non-ok\n   448\t   outcome is a reasoned terminal failure: a reflection can answer\n   449\t   `not-found` or `channel-gone` while minting a cursor\n   450\t   (dao.stream.remote.cljc's `refl-cursor`), and that must not be\n   451\t   mistaken for still-pending.  Returns `[status cursor result]`, status\n   452\t   one of `:ok`, `:retry`, `:terminal`; `result` is retained for\n   453\t   diagnostics either way.\"\n   454\t  [reader anchor]\n   455\t  (let [r (stream/cursor reader anchor)\n   456\t        outcome (:dao.stream/outcome r)]\n   457\t    (cond\n   458\t      (= :dao.stream/ok outcome) [:ok (:dao.stream/cursor r) r]\n   459\t\n   460\t      (and (= :dao.stream/transport-error outcome) (:dao.stream/retry? r))\n   461\t      [:retry anchor r]\n   462\t\n   463\t      :else [:terminal anchor r])))\n   464\t\n   465\t\n   466\t(defn- poll-read\n   467\t  [state]\n   468\t  (let [read-result (valid-operation-result :next (stream/next (:reader state) (:cursor state)))\n   469\t        outcome (:dao.stream/outcome read-result)]\n   470\t    (case outcome\n   471\t      :dao.stream/ok\n   472\t      ;; Advance before decoding. A malformed or unsolicited element is thereby\n   473\t      ;; consumed exactly once and cannot poison polling.\n   474\t      (handle-event (assoc state :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor read-result))\n   475\t                    (decode-value state (:dao.stream/value read-result)))\n   476\t\n   477\t      :dao.stream/blocked\n   478\t      (rpc-result :dao.stream.rpc/idle state :dao.stream.rpc/read read-result)\n   479\t\n   480\t      :dao.stream/gap\n   481\t      (let [state (-> state\n   482\t                      (assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor read-result))\n   483\t                      (lose-outstanding :dao.stream/gap false))]\n   484\t        (rpc-result :dao.stream.rpc/lost state\n   485\t                    :dao.stream.rpc/reason :dao.stream/gap\n   486\t                    :dao.stream.rpc/read read-result))\n   487\t\n   488\t      (terminal-lost state read-result))))\n   489\t\n   490\t\n   491\t(defn poll!\n   492\t  \"Read at most `budget` response-medium elements.\n   493\t\n   494\t   A `:dao.stream/blocked` result yields immediately; this function never loops\n   495\t   waiting for a response.  Each successful read installs the exact successor\n   496\t   cursor returned by that handle before decoding the element.\"\n   497\t  ([state] (poll! state 1))\n   498\t  ([state budget]\n   499\t   (cond\n   500\t     (:terminal state) (rpc-result :dao.stream.rpc/terminal state)\n   501\t     (not (and (integer? budget) (pos? budget)))\n   502\t     (rpc-result :dao.stream.rpc/idle state)\n   503\t     :else\n   504\t     (loop [remaining budget\n   505\t            state state\n   506\t            last-result nil]\n   507\t       (cond\n   508\t         (zero? remaining) (or last-result (rpc-result :dao.stream.rpc/idle state))\n   509\t\n   510\t         ;; The response cursor is an unresolved anchor: settling it is not\n   511\t         ;; a read and does not spend the budget, exactly as\n   512\t         ;; dao.jing.content.step/poll's own anchor branch does not.\n   513\t         (contains? stream/standard-anchors (:cursor state))\n   514\t         (let [[status cursor r] (mint-cursor (:reader state) (:cursor state))]\n   515\t           (case status\n   516\t             :ok (recur remaining (assoc state :cursor cursor) last-result)\n   517\t             :retry (or last-result\n   518\t                        (rpc-result :dao.stream.rpc/idle state :dao.stream.rpc/read r))\n   519\t             :terminal (terminal-lost state r)))\n   520\t\n   521\t         :else\n   522\t         (let [result (poll-read state)\n   523\t               next-state (:dao.stream.rpc/state result)\n   524\t               outcome (:dao.stream.rpc/outcome result)]\n   525\t           (if (or (:terminal next-state)\n   526\t                   (= outcome :dao.stream.rpc/idle))\n   527\t             result\n   528\t             (recur (dec remaining) next-state result))))))))\n   529\t\n   530\t\n   531\t(defn take-completed\n   532\t  \"Return `[completions next-state]`, clearing the unpublished completion\n   533\t   outbox exactly once.  The caller owns publication and must call this only\n   534\t   from its single state-owning driver step.\"\n   535\t  [state]\n   536\t  [(:completed state) (assoc state :completed [])])\n   537\t\n   538\t\n   539\t(defn take-diagnostics\n   540\t  \"Return `[diagnostics next-state]`, clearing the unpublished diagnostic outbox\n   541\t   exactly once.  Diagnostics are bounded by publication exactly as completions\n   542\t   are: a noisy shared response medium can produce one per read, so a caller\n   543\t   that never publishes would grow this vector for the session's lifetime.\"\n   544\t  [state]\n   545\t  [(:diagnostics state) (assoc state :diagnostics [])])\n   546\t\n   547\t\n   548\t(defn rebind\n   549\t  \"Replace a detached client's writer (and optionally reader) without creating\n   550\t   a cursor or replacing the random id allocator. Only `/detached` is\n   551\t   reconnectable; other terminal reasons remain terminal.\"\n   552\t  ([state writer]\n   553\t   (if (= :dao.stream.apply/detached (:terminal state))\n   554\t     (assoc state :writer writer :terminal nil)\n   555\t     state))\n   556\t  ([state writer reader]\n   557\t   (if (= :dao.stream.apply/detached (:terminal state))\n   558\t     (assoc state :writer writer :reader reader :terminal nil)\n   559\t     state)))\n   380\t\n   381\t(defn- drain-lifecycle\n   382\t  \"Read the lifecycle medium, total over every `next` outcome.  A gap is a fatal\n   383\t   endpoint-observability failure and triggers shutdown, per R4.\"\n   384\t  [endpoint]\n   385\t  (loop [remaining lifecycle-budget\n   386\t         endpoint endpoint]\n   387\t    (if (or (zero? remaining) (nil? (:lifecycle-cursor endpoint)))\n   388\t      endpoint\n   389\t      (let [result (stream/next (:lifecycle endpoint) (:lifecycle-cursor endpoint))\n   390\t            outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n   391\t        (case outcome\n   392\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   393\t          (let [envelope (:dao.stream/value result)\n   394\t                kind (get envelope event-key)\n   395\t                endpoint (assoc endpoint\n   396\t                                :lifecycle-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n   397\t                                :lifecycle-ledger outcome)]\n   398\t            (recur (dec remaining)\n   399\t                   (lifecycle-transition endpoint\n   400\t                                         (when (contains? event-kinds kind) kind)\n   401\t                                         (get envelope value-key))))\n   402\t\n   403\t          :dao.stream/gap\n   404\t          (-> endpoint\n   405\t              (assoc :lifecycle-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n   406\t                     :lifecycle-ledger outcome)\n   407\t              (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   408\t                       \";; endpoint lifecycle lost: observability failed, stopping\")\n   409\t              stop!)\n   410\t\n   411\t          :dao.stream/blocked\n   412\t          (assoc endpoint :lifecycle-ledger outcome)\n   413\t\n   414\t          (-> endpoint\n   415\t              (assoc :lifecycle-ledger outcome)\n   416\t              (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   417\t                       (str \";; endpoint lifecycle \" (name outcome)))))))))\n   418\t\n   419\t\n   420\t;; =============================================================================\n   421\t;; Requests\n   422\t;; =============================================================================\n   423\t\n   424\t(defn- evaluate\n   425\t  \"Answer one validated request against the one shared shell, serially.\"\n   426\t  [repl request]\n   427\t  (let [id (rpc/request-id request)]\n   428\t    (cond\n   429\t      (not= eval-operation (rpc/request-op request))\n   430\t      [repl (rpc/error-answer id :yin.repl.serve/unknown-operation\n   431\t                              \"This endpoint answers :op/eval only; it does not proxy\")]\n   432\t\n   433\t      (not (string? (first (rpc/request-args request))))\n   434\t      [repl (rpc/error-answer id :yin.repl.serve/invalid-arguments\n   435\t                              \"An :op/eval request carries one source string\")]\n   436\t\n   437\t      :else\n   438\t      (try\n   439\t        (let [[repl' text] (repl/eval-input repl (first (rpc/request-args request)))]\n   440\t          (if (:pending-input repl')\n   441\t            ;; Line continuation is a terminal concern.  One shared shell means\n   442\t            ;; an unbalanced request would otherwise prefix the *next*\n   443\t            ;; caller's source, so the fragment is refused and dropped here\n   444\t            ;; rather than retained across a caller boundary.  The envelope\n   445\t            ;; was well formed, so the refusal is this server's decision and\n   446\t            ;; carries this server's code: a client can tell it from a codec\n   447\t            ;; defect.\n   448\t            [(assoc repl' :pending-input nil)\n   449\t             (rpc/error-answer id incomplete-input-code\n   450\t                               \"Incomplete input: a request carries one complete form\")]\n   451\t            [repl' (rpc/success-answer id text)]))\n   452\t        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   453\t          [repl (rpc/error-answer id :yin.repl.serve/handler-error \"Handler failed\")])))))\n   454\t\n   455\t\n   456\t(defn- deliver-answer\n   457\t  \"Append one retained answer, advancing the requests cursor only when the\n   458\t   append is accepted.  `full` retries the identical answer on a later step\n   459\t   without re-running the handler.\"\n   460\t  [endpoint]\n   461\t  (let [result (stream/append! (:answers endpoint) (:pending-answer endpoint))\n   462\t        outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n   463\t    (case outcome\n   464\t      :dao.stream/ok\n   465\t      (assoc endpoint\n   466\t             :requests-cursor (:pending-successor endpoint)\n   467\t             :pending-answer nil\n   468\t             :pending-successor nil)\n   469\t\n   470\t      :dao.stream/full\n   471\t      endpoint\n   472\t\n   473\t      (-> endpoint\n   474\t          (assoc :requests-cursor (:pending-successor endpoint)\n   475\t                 :pending-answer nil\n   476\t                 :pending-successor nil)\n   477\t          (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   478\t                   (str \";; answer undeliverable: \" (name outcome)))))))\n   479\t\n   480\t\n   481\t(defn- advance-requests\n   482\t  \"One bounded sweep of the shared requests/answers pair: a pending answer\n   483\t   is retried first (its retry runs on the host's cadence, gated on\n   484\t   nothing), then at most `request-budget` further request/answer cycles.\n   485\t   Correlation is by the self-minted random id every request and answer\n   486\t   carries (`dao.stream.rpc`), never by which connection carried it -- the\n   487\t   mirror already answered every wire-protocol question a reflection\n   488\t   asked; this is the interpreter over the local requests/answers ends the\n   489\t   service convention names.\"\n   490\t  [endpoint]\n   491\t  (loop [remaining request-budget\n   492\t         endpoint endpoint]\n   493\t    (cond\n   494\t      (zero? remaining) endpoint\n   495\t\n   496\t      (:pending-answer endpoint)\n   497\t      (let [endpoint (deliver-answer endpoint)]\n   498\t        (if (:pending-answer endpoint)\n   499\t          endpoint\n   500\t          (recur (dec remaining) endpoint)))\n   501\t\n   502\t      :else\n   503\t      (let [result (stream/next (:requests endpoint) (:requests-cursor endpoint))\n   504\t            outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n   505\t        (case outcome\n   506\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   507\t          (let [request (:dao.stream/value result)\n   508\t                successor (:dao.stream/cursor result)]\n   509\t            (cond\n   510\t              (rpc/request-value? request)\n   511\t              (let [[repl' answer] (evaluate (:repl endpoint) request)]\n   512\t                (recur remaining\n   513\t                       (assoc endpoint\n   514\t                              :repl repl'\n   515\t                              :pending-answer answer\n   516\t                              :pending-successor successor)))\n   517\t\n   518\t              ;; Correlatable but malformed: an error answer at least tells\n   519\t              ;; the caller their own request failed, distinct from silence.\n   520\t              (and (map? request) (rpc/safe-id? (:dao.stream.rpc/id request)))\n   521\t              (recur remaining\n   522\t                     (assoc endpoint\n   523\t                            :pending-answer\n   524\t                            (rpc/error-answer (:dao.stream.rpc/id request)\n   525\t                                             :yin.repl.serve/malformed-request\n   526\t                                             \"Malformed request envelope\")\n   527\t                            :pending-successor successor))\n   528\t\n   529\t              :else\n   530\t              (recur (dec remaining)\n   531\t                     (-> endpoint\n   532\t                         (assoc :requests-cursor successor)\n   533\t                         (publish :yin.repl.serve/diagnostic\n   534\t                                  \";; malformed request dropped\")))))\n   535\t\n   536\t          :dao.stream/blocked endpoint\n   537\t\n   538\t          :dao.stream/gap\n   539\t          (recur (dec remaining)\n   540\t                 (-> endpoint\n   541\t                     (assoc :requests-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result))\n   542\t                     (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   543\t                              \";; requests lost; resuming at the recovery cursor\")))\n   544\t\n   545\t          (publish endpoint :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   546\t                   (str \";; requests \" (name outcome))))))))\n   547\t\n   548\t\n   549\t;; =============================================================================\n   550\t;; Stop\n   551\t;; =============================================================================\n   552\t\n   553\t(defn stopped?\n   554\t  \"True when nothing more is owed to this endpoint's shutdown: it reported\n   555\t   `:stopped`, or it never composed an acceptor at all.\n   556\t\n   557\t   A refused bind configuration or a missing host package leaves an endpoint\n   558\t   that owns its media and its reason and nothing else.  No host close\n   559\t   completion exists to deposit `:stopped` for it, so a shutdown that waited for\n   560\t   one would spend its whole budget and then report a timeout for a listener\n   561\t   that never bound.\"\n   562\t  [endpoint]\n   563\t  (or (nil? endpoint)\n   564\t      (= :stopped (:status endpoint))\n   565\t      (nil? (:acceptor endpoint))))\n   566\t\n   567\t\n   568\t(defn stop!\n   569\t  \"Initiate stop, claiming nothing about completion.\n   570\t\n   571\t   Closing the shared requests and answers media is what makes a connected\n   572\t   client observe `:dao.stream/end` -- the bare source outcome the mirror\n   573\t   relays verbatim -- on its next read, translated to `:dao.stream.apply/\n   574\t   ended`: a permanent conclusion, never a reattachable detach.  Every\n   575\t   accepted session's own socket closes later, in `finish-stop`, once this\n   576\t   step's mirror pass has had the chance to deliver that answer over the\n   577\t   wire; closing it here would race that delivery.  Only the host close\n   578\t   completion deposits `:stopped`, and only `step` consuming it marks the\n   579\t   stop complete and releases the resolution-table entry.\n   580\t\n   581\t   An endpoint with no acceptor is left exactly as it is: it holds no\n   582\t   listener and no attachment, so there is nothing to initiate, and marking it\n   583\t   `:stopping` would both claim a stop nobody can complete and erase the status\n   584\t   that says why it never started.\"\n   585\t  [endpoint]\n   586\t  (if (or (contains? #{:stopping :stopped} (:status endpoint))\n   587\t          (nil? (:acceptor endpoint)))\n   588\t    endpoint\n   589\t    (do\n   590\t      (stream/close! (:answers endpoint))\n   591\t      (stream/close! (:requests endpoint))\n   592\t      (assoc endpoint :status :stopping))))\n   593\t\n   594\t\n   595\t(def stop-grace-ms\n   596\t  \"How long, in the caller's clock domain, `finish-stop` waits after\n   597\t   `stop!` closed the shared requests/answers media before it closes any\n   598\t   accepted session's socket.  Closing the socket too soon would race the\n   599\t   wire answer a client's outstanding read of the now-ended media is\n   600\t   owed: that read answers with the media's own `:dao.stream/end`, and\n   601\t   the client must see that -- `:ended`, never reattachable -- before its\n   602\t   socket also reports `:ws/closed`, which alone would read as a\n   603\t   reattachable detach.  A fixed step count cannot bound this: it says\n   604\t   nothing about the client's own independent poll cadence or the network\n   605\t   round trip its read takes.\"\n   606\t  500)\n   607\t\n   608\t\n   609\t(defn- finish-stop*\n   610\t  [endpoint]\n   611\t  (if (:stop-initiated? endpoint)\n   612\t    endpoint\n   613\t    (let [endpoint (assoc endpoint :stop-initiated? true)\n   614\t          endpoint (do (doseq [[_ session] (ws-project/sessions (:acceptor endpoint))]\n   615\t                         (stream/close! (:handle session)))\n   616\t                       endpoint)\n   617\t          bound @(:resources endpoint)\n   618\t          result\n   619\t          (if bound\n   620\t            (try\n   621\t              ((:unbind! (:host endpoint)) bound (:deposit! endpoint))\n   622\t              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}\n   623\t              (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   624\t                (let [reason {:code :yin.repl.endpoint/unbind-threw\n   625\t                              :message \"the host listener failed to release\"}]\n   626\t                  ((:deposit! endpoint) :listener-error reason)\n   627\t                  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   628\t                   :dao.stream/diagnostic reason})))\n   629\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   630\t             :dao.stream/diagnostic\n   631\t             {:code :yin.repl.endpoint/never-bound\n   632\t              :message \"the host listener never returned a resource\"}})]\n   633\t      (if (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n   634\t        ;; A synchronous release failure has no later host completion to\n   635\t        ;; observe.  The composition owns that fact and resolves locally,\n   636\t        ;; retaining the structured reason in the ordinary notice stream.\n   637\t        (-> endpoint\n   638\t            (assoc :status :stopped :resolution nil)\n   639\t            (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   640\t                     (str \"Endpoint stopped without host completion: \"\n   641\t                          (pr-str (data/summarize (:dao.stream/diagnostic result)\n   642\t                                                  diagnostic-bounds)))))\n   643\t        endpoint))))\n   644\t\n   645\t\n   646\t(defn- finish-stop\n   647\t  [endpoint now]\n   648\t  (cond\n   649\t    (not= :stopping (:status endpoint)) endpoint\n   650\t    (nil? (:acceptor endpoint)) endpoint\n   651\t\n   652\t    ;; Nothing to wait for: skip the grace period entirely rather than\n   653\t    ;; delay a stop with no accepted session to deliver anything to.\n   654\t    (empty? (ws-project/sessions (:acceptor endpoint))) (finish-stop* endpoint)\n   655\t\n   656\t    ;; Real elapsed time, not a step count: a fixed number of this\n   657\t    ;; endpoint's own ticks says nothing about whether a client's\n   658\t    ;; independent poll cadence -- and the network round trip its own\n   659\t    ;; read takes -- has actually had the chance to run in that time.\n   660\t    (nil? (:stop-requested-at endpoint))\n   661\t    (assoc endpoint :stop-requested-at now)\n   662\t\n   663\t    (< (- now (:stop-requested-at endpoint)) stop-grace-ms)\n   664\t    endpoint\n   665\t\n   666\t    :else\n   667\t    (finish-stop* endpoint)))\n   668\t\n   669\t\n   670\t;; =============================================================================\n   671\t;; The driver step\n   672\t;; =============================================================================\n   673\t\n   674\t(defn step\n   675\t  \"Advance the endpoint once at `now`, returning the next endpoint value.\n   676\t\n   677\t   Ordering is intentional: lifecycle first, so a bind result is known before\n   678\t   anything claims to be serving; then the accepting composition's own\n   679\t   transport/offer/mirror step; then one bounded sweep of the shared\n   680\t   requests/answers pair against the single shared REPL state.\"\n   681\t  [endpoint now]\n   682\t  (if-not endpoint\n   683\t    endpoint\n   684\t    (let [outbox-before (count (:outbox endpoint))\n   685\t          endpoint (drain-lifecycle endpoint)]\n   686\t      (if-not (:acceptor endpoint)\n   687\t        ;; An endpoint that never composed an acceptor -- a refused bind\n   688\t        ;; configuration or a missing host package -- still owns and reports\n   689\t        ;; its lifecycle medium; it simply has no requests to advance.\n   690\t        endpoint\n   691\t        (let [before (set (keys (ws-project/sessions (:acceptor endpoint))))\n   692\t              _ (ws-project/accept-step! (:acceptor endpoint) now)\n   693\t              departed (remove (ws-project/sessions (:acceptor endpoint)) before)\n   694\t              endpoint (reduce (fn [endpoint attachment]\n   695\t                                 (publish endpoint :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   696\t                                          (str \";; attachment \" attachment \" left\")))\n   697\t                               endpoint departed)\n   698\t              cursor-before (:requests-cursor endpoint)\n   699\t              endpoint (advance-requests endpoint)]\n   700\t          (-> endpoint\n   701\t              (assoc :step-moved?\n   702\t                     (boolean (or (some? (:pending-answer endpoint))\n   703\t                                 (not= cursor-before (:requests-cursor endpoint))\n   704\t                                 (> (count (:outbox endpoint)) outbox-before))))\n   705\t              (finish-stop now)))))))\n   706\t\n   707\t\n   708\t(defn moved?\n   709\t  \"True when the last `step` moved something a caller's cadence must not\n   710\t   sleep through: a notice was published, or a computed answer still owes\n   711\t   an append, which must never wait out a backoff ceiling.\"\n   712\t  [endpoint]\n   713\t  (boolean (or (:step-moved? endpoint) (:pending-answer endpoint))))\n   714\t\n   715\t\n   716\t(defn summary\n   717\t  \"A serializable summary of endpoint state, for `(repl-state)` and tests.\"\n   718\t  [endpoint]\n   719\t  (when endpoint\n   720\t    {:status (:status endpoint)\n   721\t     :url (url endpoint)\n   722\t     :path (:path endpoint)\n   723\t     :identity (:dao.stream/identity (:descriptor endpoint))\n   724\t     :serving? (some? (:resolution endpoint))\n   725\t     :sessions (if (:acceptor endpoint)\n   726\t                (vec (sort (keys (ws-project/sessions (:acceptor endpoint)))))\n   727\t                [])\n   728\t     :lifecycle {:cursor (:lifecycle-cursor endpoint)\n   729\t                 :last-outcome (:lifecycle-ledger endpoint)}}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/adapter.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc | sed -n '1,420p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/adapter.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc | sed -n '1,420p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.adapter\n     2\t  \"A small, host-neutral bridge between a line-oriented Yin REPL and the\n     3\t   DaoStream RPC state machine.\n     4\t\n     5\t   This is deliberately not a replacement for `yin.repl`: it does not create a\n     6\t   socket, evaluate a form, print, own an atom, or invoke a callback.  A driver\n     7\t   owns the state returned here.  Local shell commands are emitted as data for\n     8\t   that driver to evaluate locally; every other input string becomes one\n     9\t   `:op/eval` request through the explicit RPC client state.\"\n    10\t  (:require #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    11\t               :clj [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    12\t               :cljs [cljs.reader :as reader])\n    13\t            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]))\n    14\t\n    15\t\n    16\t(def eval-operation :op/eval)\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\t(def local-command-heads\n    20\t  \"Commands which retain the legacy REPL's local meaning when a remote RPC\n    21\t   client is present.  The adapter emits their original input; it does not\n    22\t   interpret or execute them.\"\n    23\t  #{'connect 'disconnect 'help 'quit 'repl-state})\n    24\t\n    25\t\n    26\t(def rejected-command-heads\n    27\t  \"Commands the REPL does not have.  `(telemetry)` is out in every form, so\n    28\t   the adapter names the rejection as an event rather than doing nothing locally\n    29\t   or sending the line to a remote evaluator that would report it as a missing\n    30\t   var.\"\n    31\t  #{'telemetry})\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\t(defn state\n    35\t  \"Create adapter state around explicit, caller-owned RPC client state.\n    36\t   `:events` is an unpublished outbox; use `take-events` to consume it once.\"\n    37\t  [rpc-state]\n    38\t  {:yin.repl.adapter/rpc rpc-state\n    39\t   :yin.repl.adapter/events []})\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(def init-state state)\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\t(defn eval-request\n    46\t  \"Construct the request value used for a non-local input.  Normal callers\n    47\t   use `submit-input`, which delegates id allocation and append handling to\n    48\t   RPC.\"\n    49\t  [id input]\n    50\t  (rpc/request-value id eval-operation [input]))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(defn- read-forms\n    54\t  \"Read the line with a non-evaluating reader on every host.  Sniffing an input\n    55\t   line for a shell command must never run it; anything the data reader rejects\n    56\t   is ordinary source for the remote evaluator.\"\n    57\t  [input]\n    58\t  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n    59\t     :clj (edn/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n    60\t     :cljs (reader/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))))\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\t(defn command-form\n    64\t  \"Exactly one well-formed shell-command form, otherwise nil.  Reader failures\n    65\t   intentionally mean remote input: ordinary language source must reach the\n    66\t   remote evaluator unchanged.\"\n    67\t  [input]\n    68\t  (when (string? input)\n    69\t    (try\n    70\t      (let [forms (read-forms input)\n    71\t            form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n    72\t        (when (and (seq? form) (symbol? (first form))) form))\n    73\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\t(defn- command-head\n    77\t  \"The head symbol of one well-formed shell-command form, otherwise nil.\"\n    78\t  [input]\n    79\t  (first (command-form input)))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(defn local-command\n    83\t  \"Return the local command symbol for one well-formed local shell command,\n    84\t   otherwise nil.\"\n    85\t  [input]\n    86\t  (let [head (command-head input)]\n    87\t    (when (contains? local-command-heads head) head)))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn rejected-command\n    91\t  \"Return the command symbol for one well-formed command this slice rejects,\n    92\t   otherwise nil.\"\n    93\t  [input]\n    94\t  (let [head (command-head input)]\n    95\t    (when (contains? rejected-command-heads head) head)))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(defn- adapter-result\n    99\t  [outcome state & {:as extra}]\n   100\t  (merge {:yin.repl.adapter/outcome outcome\n   101\t          :yin.repl.adapter/state state}\n   102\t         extra))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t(defn- append-event\n   106\t  [state event]\n   107\t  (update state :yin.repl.adapter/events conj event))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(defn- request-outcome\n   111\t  [rpc-outcome]\n   112\t  (case rpc-outcome\n   113\t    :dao.stream.rpc/requested :yin.repl.adapter/requested\n   114\t    :dao.stream.rpc/pending-request :yin.repl.adapter/pending-request\n   115\t    :dao.stream.rpc/request-undeliverable :yin.repl.adapter/request-undeliverable\n   116\t    :dao.stream.rpc/invalid-request :yin.repl.adapter/invalid-input\n   117\t    :dao.stream.rpc/allocator-error :yin.repl.adapter/terminal\n   118\t    :dao.stream.rpc/terminal :yin.repl.adapter/terminal\n   119\t    :yin.repl.adapter/transport-result))\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\t(defn submit-input\n   123\t  \"Advance one input transition.\n   124\t\n   125\t   A local command becomes an explicit event and leaves RPC state untouched, as\n   126\t   does a command this slice rejects.  Other strings are submitted as a\n   127\t   `:op/eval` request.  This function makes at\n   128\t   most one append attempt through `rpc/request!`; it never waits or retries.\"\n   129\t  [state input]\n   130\t  (cond\n   131\t    (not (string? input))\n   132\t    (let [event {:yin.repl.adapter/event :yin.repl.adapter/invalid-input\n   133\t                 :yin.repl.adapter/input input}\n   134\t          state (append-event state event)]\n   135\t      (adapter-result :yin.repl.adapter/invalid-input state\n   136\t                      :yin.repl.adapter/event event))\n   137\t\n   138\t    (rejected-command input)\n   139\t    (let [command (rejected-command input)\n   140\t          event {:yin.repl.adapter/event :yin.repl.adapter/rejected-command\n   141\t                 :yin.repl.adapter/command command\n   142\t                 :yin.repl.adapter/input input}\n   143\t          state (append-event state event)]\n   144\t      (adapter-result :yin.repl.adapter/rejected-command state\n   145\t                      :yin.repl.adapter/event event))\n   146\t\n   147\t    (local-command input)\n   148\t    (let [command (local-command input)\n   149\t          event {:yin.repl.adapter/event :yin.repl.adapter/local-command\n   150\t                 :yin.repl.adapter/command command\n   151\t                 :yin.repl.adapter/input input}\n   152\t          state (append-event state event)]\n   153\t      (adapter-result :yin.repl.adapter/local-command state\n   154\t                      :yin.repl.adapter/event event))\n   155\t\n   156\t    :else\n   157\t    (let [rpc-result (rpc/request! (:yin.repl.adapter/rpc state)\n   158\t                                   eval-operation\n   159\t                                   [input])\n   160\t          state (assoc state :yin.repl.adapter/rpc\n   161\t                       (:dao.stream.rpc/state rpc-result))]\n   162\t      (adapter-result (request-outcome (:dao.stream.rpc/outcome rpc-result))\n   163\t                      state\n   164\t                      :yin.repl.adapter/rpc-result rpc-result))))\n   165\t\n   166\t\n   167\t(defn- completion-event\n   168\t  [completion]\n   169\t  (let [base {:yin.repl.adapter/id (:dao.stream.rpc/id completion)\n   170\t              :yin.repl.adapter/op (:dao.stream.rpc/op completion)\n   171\t              :yin.repl.adapter/args (:dao.stream.rpc/args completion)}]\n   172\t    (if-let [response (:dao.stream.rpc/response completion)]\n   173\t      (if (rpc/answer-ok? response)\n   174\t        (assoc base\n   175\t               :yin.repl.adapter/event :yin.repl.adapter/response\n   176\t               :yin.repl.adapter/value (rpc/answer-ok response))\n   177\t        (assoc base\n   178\t               :yin.repl.adapter/event :yin.repl.adapter/response\n   179\t               :yin.repl.adapter/error (rpc/answer-error response)))\n   180\t      (assoc base\n   181\t             :yin.repl.adapter/event :yin.repl.adapter/lost\n   182\t             :yin.repl.adapter/reason (:dao.stream.rpc/reason completion)))))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn publish-completions\n   186\t  \"Move RPC's completion outbox into the REPL event outbox exactly once.\n   187\t   The returned RPC state has an empty completion vector, so a later driver tick\n   188\t   cannot publish the same correlated response or loss again.\"\n   189\t  [state]\n   190\t  (let [[completions rpc-state] (rpc/take-completed (:yin.repl.adapter/rpc state))\n   191\t        events (mapv completion-event completions)\n   192\t        state (-> state\n   193\t                  (assoc :yin.repl.adapter/rpc rpc-state)\n   194\t                  (update :yin.repl.adapter/events into events))]\n   195\t    (adapter-result (if (seq events)\n   196\t                      :yin.repl.adapter/published\n   197\t                      :yin.repl.adapter/idle)\n   198\t                    state\n   199\t                    :yin.repl.adapter/events events)))\n   200\t\n   201\t\n   202\t(defn poll-responses\n   203\t  \"Poll up to `budget` response values, then publish any correlated completion\n   204\t   values as REPL events.  `:blocked` returns immediately through `rpc/poll!`.\n   205\t   No host asynchronous value, callback, or scheduler is introduced.\"\n   206\t  ([state] (poll-responses state 1))\n   207\t  ([state budget]\n   208\t   (let [rpc-result (rpc/poll! (:yin.repl.adapter/rpc state) budget)\n   209\t         state (assoc state :yin.repl.adapter/rpc\n   210\t                      (:dao.stream.rpc/state rpc-result))\n   211\t         published (publish-completions state)\n   212\t         state (:yin.repl.adapter/state published)\n   213\t         rpc-outcome (:dao.stream.rpc/outcome rpc-result)\n   214\t         outcome (cond\n   215\t                   (seq (:yin.repl.adapter/events published))\n   216\t                   :yin.repl.adapter/responded\n   217\t\n   218\t                   (= rpc-outcome :dao.stream.rpc/idle)\n   219\t                   :yin.repl.adapter/idle\n   220\t\n   221\t                   (= rpc-outcome :dao.stream.rpc/terminal)\n   222\t                   :yin.repl.adapter/terminal\n   223\t\n   224\t                   :else :yin.repl.adapter/transport-result)]\n   225\t     (adapter-result outcome state\n   226\t                     :yin.repl.adapter/rpc-result rpc-result\n   227\t                     :yin.repl.adapter/events\n   228\t                     (:yin.repl.adapter/events published)))))\n   229\t\n   230\t\n   231\t(defn take-events\n   232\t  \"Return `[events next-state]`, clearing the adapter event outbox exactly once.\n   233\t   Drivers interpret local-command events locally and render response/loss events\n   234\t   in their own host loop.\"\n   235\t  [state]\n   236\t  [(:yin.repl.adapter/events state)\n   237\t   (assoc state :yin.repl.adapter/events [])])\n     1\t(ns dao.stream.ws-project\n     2\t  \"The WebSocket channel composition of dao.stream.remote.md (3.1).\n     3\t\n     4\t   The mirror and the link of dao.stream.remote speak raw request and\n     5\t   answer maps, so each channel end composes one step, the projection,\n     6\t   between the ws deposit medium and the channel: the channel reader is\n     7\t   a ring buffer the composition wires, the channel writer is the ws\n     8\t   handle itself. The projection holds the reading cursor on the\n     9\t   attachment's traffic medium, keeps the events whose :ws/attachment\n    10\t   names this channel, appends the :ws/value of each :ws/payload onto\n    11\t   the ring, and drops :ws/error diagnostics. A terminal lifecycle\n    12\t   event (:ws/closed, :ws/ended) or a failure resolution (:ws/not-found,\n    13\t   :ws/transport-error) makes the projection close the ring, and so\n    14\t   does the traffic medium's own end: the projection is over and\n    15\t   nothing more can arrive, so a link waiting on the ring observes the\n    16\t   loss instead of blocking forever -- channel loss is then the link's\n    17\t   own end observation (2.4).\n    18\t\n    19\t   The composition helpers wire both ends of the spec's section-5 toy\n    20\t   over real attachments. The accepting peer drives `accept-step!`:\n    21\t   endpoint steps, one offer adopted per tick (a fresh traffic medium\n    22\t   and ring per accepted connection, acknowledged per dao.stream.ws.md\n    23\t   Serving), then per session the projection and, over the projected\n    24\t   reader and the socket handle, dao.stream.remote/mirror-step. The\n    25\t   dialing peer composes `dial` over one ws attacher and drives\n    26\t   `dial-step!`: the projection and then its own mirror step, so either\n    27\t   peer serves the other on one connection. Reflections come from\n    28\t   dao.stream.remote/attacher through the channel end each side holds.\n    29\t   Every step here is driver-paced: the composition owns the cadence,\n    30\t   as it does for endpoint-step. Nothing schedules itself.\"\n    31\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n    32\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n    33\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]))\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(def terminal-events\n    37\t  \"The deposited events that end the channel: a terminal lifecycle\n    38\t   event for the attachment (:ws/closed, :ws/ended) or a failure\n    39\t   resolution (:ws/not-found, :ws/transport-error). The projection\n    40\t   closes the ring on each of them. :ws/error is a diagnostic and is\n    41\t   never terminal by itself (dao.stream.ws.md, Deposited events are\n    42\t   envelopes).\"\n    43\t  #{:ws/closed :ws/ended :ws/not-found :ws/transport-error})\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t;; =============================================================================\n    47\t;; The projection (3.1's ws-project step)\n    48\t;; =============================================================================\n    49\t\n    50\t(defn projection\n    51\t  \"Compose one projection over the attachment named `:attachment` (the\n    52\t   :ws/attachment value every deposited event of this channel carries),\n    53\t   the traffic medium reader `:traffic`, the already-minted reading\n    54\t   cursor `:cursor`, and the ring buffer `:ring` the channel reads.\n    55\t   The projection owns the cursor from here: each `step!` advances it.\"\n    56\t  [{:keys [attachment traffic cursor ring]}]\n    57\t  (when-not (and (some? attachment)\n    58\t                 (stream/reader? traffic)\n    59\t                 (some? cursor)\n    60\t                 (stream/reader? ring)\n    61\t                 (stream/writer? ring)\n    62\t                 (stream/closable? ring))\n    63\t    (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws projection composition\"\n    64\t                    {:attachment attachment :traffic traffic\n    65\t                     :cursor cursor :ring ring})))\n    66\t  (atom {:attachment attachment :traffic traffic :cursor cursor\n    67\t         :ring ring :closed? false}))\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\t(defn- project!\n    71\t  \"Apply one deposited event (3.1): another attachment's event and\n    72\t   every non-payload, non-terminal kind are ignored here; a :ws/error\n    73\t   is dropped as a diagnostic; a :ws/payload's :ws/value is appended\n    74\t   onto the ring; a terminal event or failure resolution closes the\n    75\t   ring. True only for the terminal case.\"\n    76\t  [state event]\n    77\t  (when (= (:ws/attachment event) (:attachment state))\n    78\t    (let [kind (:ws/event event)]\n    79\t      (cond\n    80\t        (= :ws/payload kind)\n    81\t        (do (when (contains? event :ws/value)\n    82\t              (stream/append! (:ring state) (:ws/value event)))\n    83\t            nil)\n    84\t\n    85\t        (= :ws/error kind) nil\n    86\t\n    87\t        (contains? terminal-events kind)\n    88\t        (do (stream/close! (:ring state)) true)\n    89\t\n    90\t        :else nil))))\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(defn step!\n    94\t  \"Drive the projection once, at the composition's cadence: read the\n    95\t   traffic medium to blocked, keeping, forwarding and dropping per\n    96\t   3.1, stopping at the event that closes the ring. A gap adopts the\n    97\t   medium's own recovery cursor, the lost events being lost. The\n    98\t   medium's own end closes the projection and the ring with it:\n    99\t   nothing more can arrive, so a link waiting on the ring must\n   100\t   observe the loss (2.4) rather than block forever. Returns the\n   101\t   projection.\"\n   102\t  [project]\n   103\t  (loop []\n   104\t    (let [s @project]\n   105\t      (if (:closed? s)\n   106\t        project\n   107\t        (let [r (stream/next (:traffic s) (:cursor s))]\n   108\t          (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   109\t            :dao.stream/ok\n   110\t            (let [event (:dao.stream/value r)]\n   111\t              (swap! project assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   112\t              (if (project! s event)\n   113\t                (swap! project assoc :closed? true)\n   114\t                (recur)))\n   115\t\n   116\t            :dao.stream/end\n   117\t            (do (stream/close! (:ring s))\n   118\t                (swap! project assoc :closed? true)\n   119\t                project)\n   120\t\n   121\t            :dao.stream/gap\n   122\t            (do (swap! project assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   123\t                (recur))\n   124\t\n   125\t            ;; blocked, and any read the medium refuses: stay put.\n   126\t            project))))))\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\t(defn closed?\n   130\t  \"True once the projection stopped: the ring was closed by a terminal\n   131\t   lifecycle event or a failure resolution, or the traffic medium\n   132\t   itself answered end.\"\n   133\t  [project]\n   134\t  (:closed? @project))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t(defn reading-cursor\n   138\t  \"The projection's current reading cursor on the traffic medium.\"\n   139\t  [project]\n   140\t  (:cursor @project))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t;; =============================================================================\n   144\t;; The accepting peer (section 5: accept, project, mirror)\n   145\t;; =============================================================================\n   146\t\n   147\t(defn- writer-target?\n   148\t  [x]\n   149\t  (and (map? x)\n   150\t       (stream/writer? (:dao.stream/handle x))\n   151\t       (contains? (:dao.stream/surface x) :writer)))\n   152\t\n   153\t\n   154\t(defn- valid-slot?\n   155\t  [{:keys [offer-reader offer-cursor ack-writer]}]\n   156\t  (and (stream/reader? offer-reader)\n   157\t       (some? offer-cursor)\n   158\t       (writer-target? ack-writer)))\n   159\t\n   160\t\n   161\t(defn make-acceptor\n   162\t  \"Compose the accepting end of the spec's section-5 toy.\n   163\t   `:endpoint` is a dao.stream.ws/make-endpoint value whose handoff\n   164\t   `:slots` are given here, in endpoint order, as {:offer-reader r\n   165\t   :offer-cursor c :ack-writer target} -- readers, cursors and writers\n   166\t   the composition minted before the listener started. `:table` is the\n   167\t   mirror's table (dao.stream.remote.md 2.2). `:make-media` receives\n   168\t   one accepted offer and returns the attachment's composition:\n   169\t   :traffic (the deposit target the acknowledgement carries),\n   170\t   :admission (its declaration), :reader (the traffic reader the\n   171\t   projection reads), :cursor (its minted reading cursor) and :ring\n   172\t   (the fresh channel ring buffer). The listener is the host's: it\n   173\t   calls ws/accept-connection! on this endpoint, per dao.stream.ws.md\n   174\t   Serving.\"\n   175\t  [{:keys [endpoint slots table make-media] :as config}]\n   176\t  (when-not (and (map? config)\n   177\t                 (some? endpoint)\n   178\t                 (fn? make-media)\n   179\t                 (map? table)\n   180\t                 (seq slots)\n   181\t                 (every? valid-slot? slots))\n   182\t    (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws acceptor composition\"\n   183\t                    {:config config})))\n   184\t  (atom {:endpoint endpoint\n   185\t         :slots (vec slots)\n   186\t         :table table\n   187\t         :make-media make-media\n   188\t         :offer-cursors (mapv :offer-cursor slots)\n   189\t         :sessions {}}))\n   190\t\n   191\t\n   192\t(defn- adopt!\n   193\t  \"Adopt one accepted offer as a session: create the attachment's\n   194\t   media through :make-media, acknowledge the offer per\n   195\t   dao.stream.ws.md Serving (:ws/command :ws/accept, the deposit\n   196\t   target and its admission), and register the projection, ring,\n   197\t   reading cursor and socket handle the mirror works through. An\n   198\t   offer that is not an acceptance, and an acknowledgement the slot's\n   199\t   medium refuses, close the offered handle; the slot itself is the\n   200\t   endpoint's to release.\"\n   201\t  [acceptor slot offer]\n   202\t  (let [make-media (:make-media @acceptor)\n   203\t        handle (get-in offer [:ws/handle :dao.stream/handle])\n   204\t        attachment (:ws/attachment offer)]\n   205\t    (if-not (and (= :ws/accepted (:ws/event offer))\n   206\t                 (string? attachment)\n   207\t                 (some? handle)\n   208\t                 (stream/writer? handle)\n   209\t                 (stream/closable? handle))\n   210\t      (when (stream/closable? handle)\n   211\t        (stream/close! handle))\n   212\t      (let [media (make-media offer)\n   213\t            appended (stream/append!\n   214\t                       (:dao.stream/handle (:ack-writer slot))\n   215\t                       {:ws/attachment attachment\n   216\t                        :ws/command :ws/accept\n   217\t                        :ws/deposit (:traffic media)\n   218\t                        :ws/admission (:admission media)})]\n   219\t        (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome appended))\n   220\t          (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:sessions attachment]\n   221\t                 {:attachment attachment\n   222\t                  :handle handle\n   223\t                  :ring (:ring media)\n   224\t                  :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   225\t                            (stream/cursor (:ring media)\n   226\t                                           stream/anchor-oldest))\n   227\t                  :project (projection\n   228\t                             {:attachment attachment\n   229\t                              :traffic (:reader media)\n   230\t                              :cursor (:cursor media)\n   231\t                              :ring (:ring media)})})\n   232\t          (stream/close! handle))))))\n   233\t\n   234\t\n   235\t(defn- reaped\n   236\t  \"The sessions without the closed ones. A closed session's tick just\n   237\t   ran its last mirror pass -- a closed ring forwards no further\n   238\t   request, so only what it retained could ever be answered, and that\n   239\t   pass answered what the handle accepted -- so its handle, ring and\n   240\t   projection have nothing left to do. Keeping them would grow the\n   241\t   composition without bound across repeated connections; the endpoint\n   242\t   released the connection's slot at acceptance (dao.stream.ws.md\n   243\t   Serving), and this is the composition's own bound.\"\n   244\t  [m]\n   245\t  (into {} (remove (fn [[_ s]] (closed? (:project s))) m)))\n   246\t\n   247\t\n   248\t(defn accept-step!\n   249\t  \"Advance the accepting composition one tick at `now`, in the order\n   250\t   serving compositions use: a transport step first (releasing dead\n   251\t   pendings, consuming standing acknowledgements), then one offer per\n   252\t   slot adopted with its fresh media and acknowledgement, then a\n   253\t   second transport step, so the fresh acknowledgement is consumed and\n   254\t   the accept frame is on the wire before this end answers anything,\n   255\t   then per session the projection and, over the projected reader and\n   256\t   the socket handle, the mirror step. A session whose projection has\n   257\t   closed is then removed: the mirror pass just run was its last, and\n   258\t   repeated connections must not accumulate. Returns the acceptor.\"\n   259\t  [acceptor now]\n   260\t  (let [{:keys [endpoint slots] :as s} @acceptor]\n   261\t    (ws/endpoint-step endpoint now)\n   262\t    (doseq [[index slot] (map-indexed vector slots)]\n   263\t      (let [r (stream/next (:offer-reader slot)\n   264\t                           (nth (:offer-cursors s) index))]\n   265\t        (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   266\t          (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:offer-cursors index]\n   267\t                 (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   268\t          (adopt! acceptor slot (:dao.stream/value r)))))\n   269\t    (ws/endpoint-step endpoint now)\n   270\t    (doseq [[attachment session] (:sessions @acceptor)]\n   271\t      (step! (:project session))\n   272\t      (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:sessions attachment :cursor]\n   273\t             (remote/mirror-step (:table @acceptor)\n   274\t                                 (:ring session)\n   275\t                                 (:cursor session)\n   276\t                                 (:handle session))))\n   277\t    (swap! acceptor update :sessions reaped)\n   278\t    acceptor))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t(defn sessions\n   282\t  \"The acceptor's sessions as data: attachment id -> {:attachment\n   283\t   :handle :ring :cursor :project}.\"\n   284\t  [acceptor]\n   285\t  (:sessions @acceptor))\n   286\t\n   287\t\n   288\t(defn session-end\n   289\t  \"One accepted attachment's channel end {:reader r :writer w} -- the\n   290\t   ring this end projects onto and the socket handle it writes\n   291\t   through: the entry for dao.stream.remote/attacher's\n   292\t   :dao.stream.remote/channels map at this end, so the accepting peer\n   293\t   can attach reflections of the other direction over the same\n   294\t   connection. Nil before the attachment is adopted and again once\n   295\t   its closed session is reaped.\"\n   296\t  [acceptor attachment]\n   297\t  (when-some [session (get (:sessions @acceptor) attachment)]\n   298\t    {:reader (:ring session) :writer (:handle session)}))\n   299\t\n   300\t\n   301\t;; =============================================================================\n   302\t;; The dialing peer (section 5: the link over its dialed attachment)\n   303\t;; =============================================================================\n   304\t\n   305\t(defn dial\n   306\t  \"Compose the dialing end of one WebSocket channel (3.1). `:attach!`\n   307\t   is the dao.stream.ws/make-attacher product whose :traffic deposit\n   308\t   medium is the same medium named by `:traffic` (its target), with\n   309\t   `:cursor` already minted on it before any attach!; `:ring` is the\n   310\t   channel ring buffer this end projects onto. `:table` names the\n   311\t   identities this peer serves over the dialed channel, so\n   312\t   `dial-step!` runs the projection and then this end's own mirror\n   313\t   step: the dialing end serves the other direction on the same\n   314\t   connection. `dial-attach!` takes a remote descriptor whose\n   315\t   :dao.stream/channel is this channel's ws descriptor: it attaches,\n   316\t   projects the attachment onto the ring, and answers through\n   317\t   dao.stream.remote/attacher with the channel end {:reader ring\n   318\t   :writer handle} -- the link's drain then runs inside every\n   319\t   reflection operation. One dial value carries one active\n   320\t   attachment; a reattachment composes a fresh dial with a fresh\n   321\t   cursor, as dao.stream.ws.md composes one medium per active client\n   322\t   attachment. :dao.stream.remote/events, :dao.stream.remote/resend-\n   323\t   after and :dao.stream.remote/budget pass to the attacher as its\n   324\t   policy.\"\n   325\t  [{:keys [attach! traffic cursor ring table] :as opts}]\n   326\t  (when-not (and (fn? attach!)\n   327\t                 (map? traffic)\n   328\t                 (stream/writer? (:dao.stream/handle traffic))\n   329\t                 (stream/reader? (:dao.stream/handle traffic))\n   330\t                 (some? cursor)\n   331\t                 (stream/reader? ring)\n   332\t                 (stream/writer? ring)\n   333\t                 (stream/closable? ring)\n   334\t                 (map? table))\n   335\t    (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws dial composition\"\n   336\t                    {:opts opts})))\n   337\t  (let [channel (atom nil)\n   338\t        mirror-cursor (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\n   339\t                              (stream/cursor ring stream/anchor-oldest)))\n   340\t        policy (select-keys opts [:dao.stream.remote/events\n   341\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/resend-after\n   342\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/budget])]\n   343\t    (atom {:attach! attach! :traffic traffic :cursor cursor :ring ring\n   344\t           :table table :channel channel :mirror-cursor mirror-cursor\n   345\t           :policy policy})))\n   346\t\n   347\t\n   348\t(defn dial-attach!\n   349\t  \"Attach one reflection of `descriptor` (a :dao.stream/remote\n   350\t   descriptor) through the dialed channel: the ws attach runs first,\n   351\t   the attachment's projection is composed, and the remote attacher\n   352\t   answers with the reflection -- its confirmation deferred, per\n   353\t   dao.stream.remote.md 2.4, to the descriptor probe the link sends\n   354\t   now. A channel attach that fails answers the ws attacher's own\n   355\t   outcome. One dial value carries one active attachment: a dial that\n   356\t   has already attached rejects a further dial-attach! -- its ring\n   357\t   and traffic cursor already belong to the first attachment, and a\n   358\t   second projection on them would mix two attachments' state -- with\n   359\t   a composition error; a reattachment composes a fresh dial with a\n   360\t   fresh cursor, as `dial` documents. Returns the remote attach!\n   361\t   result.\"\n   362\t  [dial descriptor]\n   363\t  (let [{:keys [attach! traffic cursor ring channel policy]} @dial]\n   364\t    (when-some [attached @channel]\n   365\t      (throw (ex-info\n   366\t               \"this dial already attached its one active attachment\"\n   367\t               {:attachment (:attachment attached)\n   368\t                :reattachment \"compose a fresh dial with a fresh cursor\"})))\n   369\t    (let [r (attach! (:dao.stream/channel descriptor))]\n   370\t      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   371\t        r\n   372\t        (let [cd (:dao.stream/channel descriptor)\n   373\t              handle (:dao.stream/handle r)\n   374\t              project (projection {:attachment (:dao.stream/attachment r)\n   375\t                                   :traffic (:dao.stream/handle traffic)\n   376\t                                   :cursor cursor\n   377\t                                   :ring ring})\n   378\t              reflect! (remote/attacher\n   379\t                         (merge policy\n   380\t                                {:dao.stream.remote/channels\n   381\t                                 {cd {:reader ring :writer handle}}}))]\n   382\t          (reset! channel {:attachment (:dao.stream/attachment r)\n   383\t                           :handle handle :project project\n   384\t                           :reflect! reflect!})\n   385\t          (reflect! descriptor))))))\n   386\t\n   387\t\n   388\t(defn dial-reflect!\n   389\t  \"Attach a further reflection of `descriptor` through a dial's already\n   390\t   established channel, sharing the one link `dial-attach!` created for\n   391\t   it: dao.stream.remote.cljc keeps one link per channel descriptor,\n   392\t   shared by every reflection through that channel, and `attacher`'s\n   393\t   returned function is exactly that per-channel sharing boundary.  A\n   394\t   dial with no established channel yet answers `:dao.stream/invalid-\n   395\t   descriptor`, since there is no attacher to share.\"\n   396\t  [dial descriptor]\n   397\t  (let [{:keys [channel]} @dial]\n   398\t    (if-some [reflect! (:reflect! @channel)]\n   399\t      (reflect! descriptor)\n   400\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor})))\n   401\t\n   402\t\n   403\t(defn dial-step!\n   404\t  \"Drive the dialing composition one tick, at the composition's\n   405\t   cadence: the attachment's projection first, so what the wire\n   406\t   deposited reaches the ring, then this end's own mirror step over\n   407\t   the projected reader and the socket handle, answering the other\n   408\t   direction's requests against this end's table. Returns the\n   409\t   mirror's advanced reading cursor.\"\n   410\t  [dial]\n   411\t  (let [{:keys [ring table channel mirror-cursor]} @dial]\n   412\t    (when-some [project (:project @channel)]\n   413\t      (step! project))\n   414\t    (when-some [handle (:handle @channel)]\n   415\t      (swap! mirror-cursor\n   416\t             (fn [c] (remote/mirror-step table ring c handle))))\n   417\t    @mirror-cursor))\n   418\t\n   419\t\n   420\t(defn channel\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
