{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/connect.cljc | sed -n '1,270p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.connect\n     2\t  \"The client side of the DaoStream Yin REPL, over the request-and-response\n     3\t   service of docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md section 5.\n     4\t\n     5\t   One connection is one explicit value.  `open` canonicalizes the URL to the\n     6\t   request-target form `dao.stream.ws.md` defines, dials one WebSocket\n     7\t   channel through `dao.stream.ws-project`, and attaches two\n     8\t   `dao.stream.remote` reflections over it -- one of `\\\"yin.repl/requests\\\"`\n     9\t   (this end writes), one of `\\\"yin.repl/answers\\\"` (this end reads) -- both\n    10\t   sharing the one link the dial establishes.  `attach!` over\n    11\t   `dao.stream.remote` answers ok at once: that is the contract's deferred\n    12\t   remote confirmation, not a promise that the server has resolved anything,\n    13\t   so a connection is reported `:established` immediately rather than\n    14\t   waiting on an asynchronous transport event.\n    15\t\n    16\t   The dial is reusable across reconnects: `close!` closes the underlying\n    17\t   channel handle, and reattaching redials the same `attach!` and repeats\n    18\t   both reflection attaches, then `rpc/rebind`s the retained RPC client onto\n    19\t   the fresh pair -- which keeps its response cursor and its outstanding\n    20\t   bookkeeping, exactly as before.  Terminal status\n    21\t   (`:detached`/`:ended`/`:not-found`/`:transport-error`) is observed from\n    22\t   the RPC client's own `:terminal`, translated by `dao.stream.rpc`'s\n    23\t   reflection-read translation; `observe-terminal` turns that into the one\n    24\t   connection notice each terminal reason publishes exactly once.\"\n    25\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    26\t            [dao.data :as data]\n    27\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    28\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    29\t            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n    30\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n    31\t            [dao.stream.ws-project :as ws-project]\n    32\t            [yin.repl.host.common :as host-common]))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t;; =============================================================================\n    36\t;; Composition constants\n    37\t;; =============================================================================\n    38\t\n    39\t(def traffic-capacity\n    40\t  \"Declared capacity of the boundary's one traffic medium, in elements.  It is\n    41\t   reused across reconnects because a client boundary has at most one active\n    42\t   attachment at a time.\"\n    43\t  8192)\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(def traffic-admission\n    47\t  {:retention :evict-oldest\n    48\t   :capacity traffic-capacity\n    49\t   :value-domain :portable-values})\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(def url-prefix \"daostream:\")\n    53\t(def ws-scheme \"ws://\")\n    54\t(def secure-scheme \"wss://\")\n    55\t(def default-port 8080)\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(def repl-path\n    59\t  \"The path an empty URL path means for this REPL (D3).  An explicit `/`\n    60\t   remains `/`; only an absent path becomes the served REPL stream.\"\n    61\t  \"/repl\")\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(def service-identity\n    65\t  \"The logical identity of the WebSocket channel a REPL endpoint serves.  A\n    66\t   descriptor names a served stream, so a client that only typed a URL still\n    67\t   needs one; a stable service name keeps `attach!` honest across endpoint\n    68\t   restarts.\"\n    69\t  \"yin.repl/repl\")\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t(def requests-identity\n    73\t  \"The mirror table identity the server enters with surface #{:writer}: a\n    74\t   client's reflection of it writes eval requests.\"\n    75\t  \"yin.repl/requests\")\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(def answers-identity\n    79\t  \"The mirror table identity the server enters with surface #{:reader}: a\n    80\t   client's reflection of it reads answers.\"\n    81\t  \"yin.repl/answers\")\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t(def ^:private diagnostic-bounds\n    85\t  \"Bound on operator-facing diagnostic text built from unbounded internal\n    86\t   state (raw connect URLs).\"\n    87\t  {:depth 3 :items 8 :chars 200})\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(def outcome-key :yin.repl.connect/outcome)\n    91\t(def connection-key :yin.repl.connect/connection)\n    92\t(def client-key :yin.repl.connect/client)\n    93\t(def descriptor-key :yin.repl.connect/descriptor)\n    94\t(def message-key :yin.repl.connect/message)\n    95\t(def event-key :yin.repl.connect/event)\n    96\t(def text-key :yin.repl.connect/text)\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t;; =============================================================================\n   100\t;; Canonical request-target paths\n   101\t;; =============================================================================\n   102\t\n   103\t(def ^:private ascii-printable\n   104\t  \" !\\\"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[\\\\]^_`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz{|}~\")\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t(def ^:private unreserved\n   108\t  (set (map str (seq \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789-._~\"))))\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\t(def ^:private hex-values\n   112\t  (merge (zipmap (map str (seq \"0123456789\")) (range 10))\n   113\t         (zipmap (map str (seq \"abcdef\")) (range 10 16))\n   114\t         (zipmap (map str (seq \"ABCDEF\")) (range 10 16))))\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(def ^:private digits (set (map str (seq \"0123456789\"))))\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(defn- at\n   121\t  \"One character of `s` as a one-character string, so nothing here depends on a\n   122\t   host's character representation.\"\n   123\t  [s i]\n   124\t  (subs s i (inc i)))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn- octet->char\n   128\t  [code]\n   129\t  (when (and (<= 32 code) (<= code 126))\n   130\t    (subs ascii-printable (- code 32) (- code 31))))\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\t(defn- percent-canonical\n   134\t  \"Decode percent-encoded unreserved octets and upper-case every remaining\n   135\t   percent hex pair.  An encoded slash is not unreserved, so it stays encoded.\"\n   136\t  [s]\n   137\t  (let [n (count s)]\n   138\t    (loop [i 0\n   139\t           out []]\n   140\t      (if (>= i n)\n   141\t        (str/join out)\n   142\t        (let [c (at s i)\n   143\t              hi (when (< (+ i 2) n) (get hex-values (at s (+ i 1))))\n   144\t              lo (when (< (+ i 2) n) (get hex-values (at s (+ i 2))))]\n   145\t          (if (and (= \"%\" c) hi lo)\n   146\t            (let [decoded (octet->char (+ (* 16 hi) lo))]\n   147\t              (if (contains? unreserved decoded)\n   148\t                (recur (+ i 3) (conj out decoded))\n   149\t                (recur (+ i 3) (conj out (str \"%\" (str/upper-case (subs s (inc i) (+ i 3))))))))\n   150\t            (recur (inc i) (conj out c))))))))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn- drop-last-segment\n   154\t  [out]\n   155\t  (if-let [i (str/last-index-of out \"/\")]\n   156\t    (subs out 0 i)\n   157\t    \"\"))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t(defn- next-segment-end\n   161\t  [s]\n   162\t  (or (str/index-of s \"/\" 1) (count s)))\n   163\t\n   164\t\n   165\t(defn- remove-dot-segments\n   166\t  \"RFC 3986's remove_dot_segments, so repeated slashes and a trailing slash stay\n   167\t   significant while `.` and `..` do not reach the exact served-path lookup.\"\n   168\t  [path]\n   169\t  (loop [in path\n   170\t         out \"\"]\n   171\t    (cond\n   172\t      (= \"\" in) out\n   173\t      (str/starts-with? in \"../\") (recur (subs in 3) out)\n   174\t      (str/starts-with? in \"./\") (recur (subs in 2) out)\n   175\t      (str/starts-with? in \"/./\") (recur (str \"/\" (subs in 3)) out)\n   176\t      (= \"/.\" in) (recur \"/\" out)\n   177\t      (str/starts-with? in \"/../\") (recur (str \"/\" (subs in 4)) (drop-last-segment out))\n   178\t      (= \"/..\" in) (recur \"/\" (drop-last-segment out))\n   179\t      (= \".\" in) (recur \"\" out)\n   180\t      (= \"..\" in) (recur \"\" out)\n   181\t      :else (let [end (next-segment-end in)]\n   182\t              (recur (subs in end) (str out (subs in 0 end)))))))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn- path-component\n   186\t  \"The URI path component of `raw`: everything before the first query or\n   187\t   fragment delimiter.\"\n   188\t  [raw]\n   189\t  (let [raw (str raw)\n   190\t        cut (->> [(str/index-of raw \"?\") (str/index-of raw \"#\")]\n   191\t                 (filter some?)\n   192\t                 (reduce min (count raw)))]\n   193\t    (subs raw 0 cut)))\n   194\t\n   195\t\n   196\t(defn canonical-path\n   197\t  \"The canonical, non-empty absolute request-target path of `raw`.\n   198\t\n   199\t   Query and fragment are ignored for lookup and absent from the descriptor,\n   200\t   dot segments are removed, percent-encoded unreserved octets are decoded, and\n   201\t   remaining percent hex digits are upper-case.  An empty URI path becomes `/`;\n   202\t   substituting the REPL's own default for an absent path is `repl-target`'s\n   203\t   job, and happens before this generic canonicalizer runs.\"\n   204\t  [raw]\n   205\t  (let [path (path-component raw)\n   206\t        path (if (str/starts-with? path \"/\") path (str \"/\" path))\n   207\t        path (percent-canonical (remove-dot-segments path))]\n   208\t    (if (= \"\" path) \"/\" path)))\n   209\t\n   210\t\n   211\t(defn repl-target\n   212\t  \"The REPL wrapper's rule: an empty raw URL path names `/repl`, and an explicit\n   213\t   `/` remains `/`.  Emptiness is a fact about the URI path component, so\n   214\t   `ws://host:port?x=1` carries no path and names `/repl` too.\"\n   215\t  [raw]\n   216\t  (if (= \"\" (path-component raw))\n   217\t    repl-path\n   218\t    (canonical-path raw)))\n   219\t\n   220\t\n   221\t;; =============================================================================\n   222\t;; URL to descriptor\n   223\t;; =============================================================================\n   224\t\n   225\t(defn- failure\n   226\t  [outcome message]\n   227\t  {outcome-key outcome message-key message})\n   228\t\n   229\t\n   230\t(defn- parse-port\n   231\t  [text]\n   232\t  (when (and (seq text) (every? #(contains? digits %) (map str (seq text))))\n   233\t    (loop [i 0 acc 0]\n   234\t      (if (>= i (count text))\n   235\t        (when (pos? acc) acc)\n   236\t        (recur (inc i) (+ (* 10 acc) (get hex-values (at text i))))))))\n   237\t\n   238\t\n   239\t(defn- authority-end\n   240\t  [s]\n   241\t  (->> [(str/index-of s \"/\") (str/index-of s \"?\") (str/index-of s \"#\")]\n   242\t       (filter some?)\n   243\t       (reduce min (count s))))\n   244\t\n   245\t\n   246\t(defn parse-url\n   247\t  \"Parse one REPL connect URL into a WebSocket descriptor.\n   248\t\n   249\t   Accepted forms are `daostream:ws://host[:port][/path]` and the same URL\n   250\t   without the `daostream:` prefix.  Bracketed IPv6 literals are out of this\n   251\t   slice and are reported rather than silently mis-parsed.\"\n   252\t  ([url] (parse-url url {}))\n   253\t  ([url {:keys [identity]}]\n   254\t   (let [url (str/trim (str url))\n   255\t         body (if (str/starts-with? url url-prefix) (subs url (count url-prefix)) url)]\n   256\t     (cond\n   257\t       (str/starts-with? body secure-scheme)\n   258\t       (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   259\t                \"wss:// has no settled descriptor form in this slice; use ws://\")\n   260\t\n   261\t       (not (str/starts-with? body ws-scheme))\n   262\t       (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   263\t                (str \"connect needs a daostream:ws:// URL; got \"\n   264\t                     (pr-str (data/summarize url diagnostic-bounds))))\n   265\t\n   266\t       :else\n   267\t       (let [rest-url (subs body (count ws-scheme))\n   268\t             end (authority-end rest-url)\n   269\t             authority (subs rest-url 0 end)\n   270\t             raw-path (subs rest-url end)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
